I actually think it's very skewed that CoMR bones are/were so common on
NAO. In a "typical" NetHack-playing environment, you'd expect a more
even mix of roles, probably; in general wizards would be higher than
many other classes because people perceive them to be easy and because
many people enjoy playing them, but on NAO there's the special
consideration of wizard typically being the best class for quite a
wide range of stupid ascension tricks. (Not least precisely because they
start with an ascension kit component in their inventory, and also,
like several but not all classes, have the ability to start with
intrinsic poison or sleep resistance, which is important for some
official and unofficial conducts.) Arguably, csaiph0 is just trying her
best to redress the balance.

(OTOH, regardless of the effects on strategy, bot bones are /usually/
boring. The most spectacularly crazy bones I know of on NAO, though,
were left by a different bot, cassaiph, who somehow got trapped in a
delicatessen and, continuously staving off short-term death without
thinking, as only a bot could, just continuously waited, keeping the
shop clear of monsters but letting them spawn elsewhere, and ate the
shop's stock or prayed when she got stuck. You can probably imagine how
the resulting bones file ended up…)


